<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 3 March, from 473 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">473 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,553 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Glycerius proclaimed Western Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Backed by the Burgundian general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gundobad">Gundobad</a>, the court official Glycerius was proclaimed emperor at Ravenna. Deposed the next year, he was one of the short-lived final rulers of the Western Empire.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1585">1585 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">441 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Teatro Olimpico opens in Vicenza</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-palladio">Andrea Palladio</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> opened with a performance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophocles">Sophocles</a>'s '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oedipus">Oedipus</a> Rex'. Its permanent painted street scenes survive, making it the oldest surviving enclosed theatre in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Continental Marines land at Nassau in the Bahamas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In their first amphibious operation, American marines and sailors captured two British forts on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-providence">New Providence</a> island, seizing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> and military stores.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Florida becomes the 27th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, acquired from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1819, was admitted to the Union as a slave state. It seceded in 1861 and is now the third most populous state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lajos Kossuth demands constitutional reform for Hungary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-diet">Hungarian Diet</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a>, Kossuth called for a responsible government and constitutional rule. His speech, made as revolution swept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, helped launch the Hungarian revolution of 1848.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-diet">Hungarian Diet</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1878">1878 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">148 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of San Stefano creates a 'Greater Bulgaria'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War</a>, the treaty created a large autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. The other great powers revised it at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> that summer, leaving lasting Balkan grievances.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Russia signs the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bolsheviks made peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a>, giving up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, the Baltic lands and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, with about a third of the old empire's population. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s defeat later voided the treaty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1923">1923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Time magazine publishes its first issue</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Founded by Henry Luce and Briton Hadden, Time summarised the week's news in a brisk, distinctive style. It became one of the most influential magazines in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rodney King's beating by Los Angeles police is filmed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A bystander videotaped officers beating Rodney King after a car chase. The officers' acquittal in April 1992 sparked riots in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> in which more than 60 people died.</p></div></li></ol>
